Company Ownership & Business Matrix

The legal architecture of Legendary Homes Limited reveals a tightly controlled structure backed by private property investors: [1]
Significant Beneficial Owners: The corporate register lists Shaoze Mo as the majority shareholder owning 75% of the company, alongside Yanjun Huang, who holds the remaining 25% stake. [1]
The Broader Network: Legendary Homes sits at the center of an interconnected development system consisting of 13 other legal entities—such as LH Opaheke Limited and Phoenix NZ Holdings Limited—used to acquire title deeds and separate risk parameters for massive land packages. [1, 2, 3]
Key Faces & Representation: While Mo and Huang hold the capital stakes, the public-facing, executive, and consultative operations are driven by figures like CJ (Shijie) Chen, who acts as a core development strategist and client partner alongside senior coordinators Lynn He, Richard Du, and Ada Liu. [1, 2]


The "Family First" Identity & Culture

A central column of the brand’s marketing and operational strategy is its "Family First" blueprint. Rather than approaching medium-density urban development through a purely commercial lens, the owners and designers explicitly market their builds under a philosophy they call “The New Architecture of Belonging” (which was heavily featured in the NZ Herald Canvas 'Silk Road Edit'). [1, 2]


The company builds homes specifically tailored for growing and multi-generational extended families, optimizing layouts to include 5-bedroom, 3-bathroom configurations that allow family members to comfortably cohabitate under one roof. This design philosophy highlights a strong connection to community-centric, family-oriented cultural dynamics. [1, 2]

Major Award Triumphs & Local Footprint

Legendary Homes has distinguished itself from standard group housing companies by securing top-tier recognition at the Registered Master Builders House of the Year competitions. Their major milestones include: [1, 2]
The Orewa Lodge Masterpiece: A hallmark project that scooped the Regional Category Winner, Regional Gold Award, and the National Category Winner at the 2020 House of the Year awards. Built initially in 2019, the home's construction prestige was validated when it resold in a slower market for over $1.9 million. [1]
Continued Dominance: The firm secured further national categories and craftsmanship accolades in the 2021 and 2023 Master Builder showcases, specifically in the Volume/Group Housing brackets. [1, 2]


Active Regional Developments

The firm continues to manage several prominent, active multi-lot suburban expansions across Auckland: [1]
North Auckland (Milldale & Upper Orewa): Recently completed an intensive 11-townhouse project on Kotiti Drive, tailoring high-spec, attainable architectural footprints for first-home buyers and extended families.
West Auckland (Huapai & Kumeu): Developing high-density duplexes and standalone footprints around Babos Avenue, fetching premium bracket pricing near local village hubs.
South Auckland (Drury & Karaka Village): Driving massive lifestyle and rural-turnkey developments at Feldspar Crossing, complete with planned boutique community spaces, eateries, and walkways. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]


